  "question": {
    "text": "The atomic masses of helium and neon are $4.0$ and $20.0$ amu respectively. The value of the de Broglie wavelength of helium gas at $-73^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ is $\\mathrm{M}$ times the de Broglie wavelength of neon at $727^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. The value of $\\mathrm{M}$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "5",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "25",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{5}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{25}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\lambda_{\\mathrm{He}}(200 \\mathrm{~K})=\\mathrm{M} \\times \\lambda_{\\mathrm{Ne}}(1000 \\mathrm{~K})$ $\\left(\\lambda=\\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{\\mathrm{m} \\cdot \\mathrm{v}}\\right)$\r\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{4 \\mathrm{amu} \\times \\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{mp}}(200)}=\\mathrm{M} \\times \\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{20 \\mathrm{amu} \\times \\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{mp}}(1000)} \\quad\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{mp}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\mathrm{KT}}{\\mathrm{m}}}\\right)$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{1}{4 \\times \\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\mathrm{~K} \\times 200}{4}}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{M}}{20 \\times \\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\mathrm{~K} \\times 1000}{20}}} \\Rightarrow \\frac{1}{4 \\times \\sqrt{50}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{M}}{20 \\times \\sqrt{50}} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{M}=5$"
  }
}